{"id": 16, "ts": 1779512440.9204621, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "agent_2", "message": "Based on the dossier and my interview notes, Candidate\u202fD shows strong alignment with several core criteria: responsibility, problem\u2011solving, concentration, and the ability to handle unexpected events\u2014key for long\u2011distance operations. However, the hot\u2011tempered demeanor and the absence of any observed evidence on crew cooperation or professional communication are notable gaps, especially given the safety\u2011critical nature of the role. In contrast, Candidate\u202fB, while reliable and stress\u2011resilient, has documented uncooperative behavior and makes nasty remarks toward colleagues, which raises similar but more concrete concerns about crew interaction. Candidate\u202fC excels in decision\u2011making and crisis calmness but has clear communication and adaptability issues. Candidate\u202fA demonstrates technical insight and leadership but is perceived as a show\u2011off and resistant to new ideas.\nGiven the current evidence, I tentatively favor Candidate\u202fD, provided we can obtain additional observations confirming that his interpersonal style does not impair crew cooperation or professional communication. I suggest we focus the next round on gathering any further insights\u2014perhaps from simulator debriefs or peer feedback\u2014regarding D\u2019s teamwork and communication behavior.\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_2\", \"vote\": \"Candidate D\"}"}
